Denial of Service (DoS) Attack: This type of attack targets a network or server, flooding it with traffic to disrupt normal business operations. The goal is to overload the system, causing it to crash or become unresponsive to legitimate users.
Distributed Denial of Service (DDoS) Attack: A DDoS attack is a more sophisticated DoS attack that uses multiple devices or servers from various locations to flood the target network, making it more likely to overwhelm the server.
